      "writtenOn": "2019-08-27T07:24:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You mean ConnectivityService#onPackageXXX() and PermissionMonitor#onPackageXXX?\n\nAs you may notice ConnectivityService#onPackageXXX() is triggered by broadcasts while PermissionMonitor#onPackageXXX is directly called by PackageManagerService synchronously during the last steps of adding/deleting/updating a package, in this way, Netd knowns about this change much quickly and avoid any unnecessary internet permission synchronization releated issues.\nJust my opinion, ^_^",
